===GREEK SENTIMENT SCALE===
+3: EXTREMELY POSITIVE
- makaria/makariotēs (blessedness), eudaimonia (supreme happiness/flourishing)
- khara megalē (great joy), nikē lampra (brilliant victory)
- olbos (divine bliss), euphrosunē (festive joy)

+2: VERY POSITIVE
- khara (joy), eudaimonia (happiness), erōs/philia/agapē (love)
- doxa (glory), kleos (fame/renown), timē (honor)
- aretē (excellence/virtue), kalos (beautiful/noble)

+1: MODERATELY POSITIVE
- eudaimōn (happy/fortunate), agathos (good), kalos (beautiful)
- elpis (hope), tharsos (courage/confidence)
- sōphrosunē (temperance/wisdom), dikaiosunē (justice)

0: NEUTRAL
- Factual statements, descriptions without emotional content
- Administrative, legal, procedural language
- Objective observations, historical narrative

-1: MODERATELY NEGATIVE
- kakos (bad), lupē (grief/pain), phobos (fear)
- anankē (necessity/constraint), ponos (toil/hardship)
- merimna (anxiety), aniā (distress)

-2: VERY NEGATIVE
- odunē (anguish), algos (pain), penthos (mourning)
- orgē/kholos/mēnis (anger/wrath), misos (hatred)
- phthonos (envy), nemesis (righteous anger)
- sumphora (disaster), kakotēs (misery)

-3: EXTREMELY NEGATIVE
- apelpisia (despair), olethros (destruction), thanatos (death)
- basanos (torture), atē (ruin/delusion)
- dustukhia (utter misfortune), kakodaimonia (wretchedness)
- ponos eschatos (extreme suffering)

INTENSIFIERS (increase sentiment):
- lian (very), malista (most), sphodra (exceedingly)
- panu (entirely), megistos (greatest)
- Superlatives: -tatos/-istos (adds +1 to base sentiment)

DIMINISHERS (decrease sentiment):
- oligon (a little), hēka (slightly), metriōs (moderately)

===IMPORTANT PARTICLES===
Greek particles carry emotional weight:
- men...de (contrast, can shift sentiment)
- ge (emphasis, intensifies)
- dē (indeed, strong assertion)
- ara (inference, realization)
- oun (therefore, conclusion)
- alla (but, strong contrast)
- kai mēn (and moreover)
- ou mēn alla (nevertheless)

===GRAMMAR CODES===
NOM=Nominative (subject)
ACC=Accusative (direct object)
GEN=Genitive (possession/source)
DAT=Dative (indirect object/means)
VOC=Vocative (address)
V=Verb
ADJ=Adjective
ADV=Adverb
CONJ=Conjunction
PREP=Preposition
PART=Participle
PRON=Pronoun
ART=Article
PTCL=Particle

